IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition (SSO informal consolidation, version in force 6/5/2026 to 20/10/2026):
-- Part 5 Division 3, s 173J -- arrangements for meetings (virtual meeting technology).
-- Layer 1 (the law, objectively). Imports the core only: the keel's `Kind of meeting` names the kinds of meeting.
-- What an answer means: JUST TRUE is yes, JUST FALSE is the text saying no in its own words, NOTHING is "the text does not say"
-- (NOTES.md, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING (sgl)"). Every fork line cited as F-n is in NOTES.md, "Fork register (sgl)".
-- The Minister's order under s 173J(7) is not encoded (machinery); its effect is an input, `the Minister has excluded ...`.

§ `Section 173J(1): the meetings the section applies to`

DECLARE `s 173J(1) meeting ordered by the Court` IS ONE OF
    `s 173J(1)(f)(i) a meeting ordered by the Court under section 182`
    `s 173J(1)(f)(ii) a meeting of creditors, members, holders of units of shares, or a class of such persons, ordered by the Court under section 210`
    `s 173J(1)(f) no meeting ordered by the Court`

-- src:15414 | 173J.—(1) This section applies to the following types of meetings:
-- src:15415 | (a) an annual general meeting of a company;
-- src:15416 | (b) an extraordinary general meeting of a company;
-- src:15417 | (c) a statutory meeting of a company;
-- src:15418 | (d) a general meeting of an amalgamating company mentioned
-- src:15419 | in section 215C or 215D;
-- src:15420 | (e) a meeting of a class of members of the company;
-- src:15421 | (f) any of the following meetings ordered by the Court, if the
-- src:15422 | Court so directs:
-- src:15423 | (i) a meeting ordered by the Court under section 182;
-- src:15424 | (ii) a meeting of creditors, members of a company,
-- src:15425 | holders of units of shares of a company, or a class of
-- src:15426 | such persons, ordered by the Court under
-- src:15427 | section 210.
@ref s 173J(1) (src:15414-15427)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of meeting`
      `the meeting is a general meeting of an amalgamating company mentioned in section 215C or 215D` IS A BOOLEAN
      `ordered` IS A `s 173J(1) meeting ordered by the Court`
      `the Court so directs that section 173J applies to the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 173J(1) the section applies to the meeting` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF kind EQUALS `an annual general meeting` OR kind EQUALS `an extraordinary general meeting`
           OR kind EQUALS `the statutory meeting` OR kind EQUALS `a meeting of a class of members`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the meeting is a general meeting of an amalgamating company mentioned in section 215C or 215D` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `ordered` EQUALS `s 173J(1)(f) no meeting ordered by the Court` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "applies to the following types of meetings" lists types and does not say "only"; a meeting of no listed type is not mentioned
        IF `the Court so directs that section 173J applies to the meeting` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(f) any of the following meetings ordered by the Court, if the Court so directs" (a meeting the Court ordered but did not so direct)

§ `Section 173J(2) and (3): how a meeting may be held`

DECLARE `s 173J(2) way of holding a meeting` IS ONE OF
    `s 173J(2)(a) at a physical place`
    `s 173J(2)(b) at a physical place and using virtual meeting technology`
    `s 173J(2)(c) using virtual meeting technology only`

-- (2) is a grant ("may be held") whose gate is "Unless excluded under subsection (5) or (7)": when the gate fails the answer is NOTHING, not
-- JUST FALSE, so that a grant is not turned into a bar (the grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 1; fork line F-1).
-- src:15429 | (2) Unless excluded under subsection (5) or (7), a meeting to which
-- src:15430 | this section applies may be held —
-- src:15432 | (a) at a physical place;
-- src:15433 | (b) at a physical place and using virtual meeting technology; or
-- src:15434 | (c) using virtual meeting technology only.
@ref s 173J(2) (src:15429-15434)
GIVEN way IS A `s 173J(2) way of holding a meeting`
      `section 173J applies to the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `subsection (5) excludes the application of paragraph (b) or (c) of subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister has by order excluded the application of subsection (2)(c) to this class of companies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 173J(2) the meeting may be held in the way` MEANS
    IF NOT `section 173J applies to the meeting`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a meeting to which this section applies may be held" -- a meeting the section does not apply to is outside the grant
    ELSE CONSIDER way
         WHEN `s 173J(2)(a) at a physical place` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 173J(2)(b) at a physical place and using virtual meeting technology` THEN
              IF `subsection (5) excludes the application of paragraph (b) or (c) of subsection (2)`
              THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Unless excluded under subsection (5) or (7), a meeting ... may be held" (F-1)
              ELSE JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 173J(2)(c) using virtual meeting technology only` THEN
              IF `subsection (5) excludes the application of paragraph (b) or (c) of subsection (2)` OR `the Minister has by order excluded the application of subsection (2)(c) to this class of companies`
              THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Unless excluded under subsection (5) or (7), a meeting ... may be held" (F-1)
              ELSE JUST TRUE

-- (3): "Where a meeting to which this section applies under subsection (2)(b) or (c) is held, the meeting may be held without any number of
-- those participating in the meeting being together at the same place." A grant gated by "Where": JUST FALSE when the meeting is not one
-- held under (2)(b) or (c), as the periods ruling's rule (b) gives it (split site (ii); fork line F-2).
-- src:15439 | (3) Where a meeting to which this section applies under
-- src:15440 | subsection (2)(b) or (c) is held, the meeting may be held without
-- src:15441 | any number of those participating in the meeting being together at the
-- src:15442 | same place.
@ref s 173J(3) (src:15439-15442)
GIVEN way IS A `s 173J(2) way of holding a meeting`
      `section 173J applies to the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 173J(3) the participants need not be together at the same place` MEANS
    IF `section 173J applies to the meeting` AND (way EQUALS `s 173J(2)(b) at a physical place and using virtual meeting technology` OR way EQUALS `s 173J(2)(c) using virtual meeting technology only`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a meeting to which this section applies under subsection (2)(b) or (c) is held" -- the meeting is not one held under (2)(b) or (c); the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b), split site (ii), F-2

§ `Section 173J(4): what a reference in the Act includes when a meeting uses virtual meeting technology`

-- The seventeen paragraphs (a) to (q) are one table: each says that "a reference in this Act to" something includes the same thing done by virtual
-- meeting technology or by the means the paragraph names. The paragraph is the typed representation; the facts say which means was used.
DECLARE `s 173J(4) paragraph` IS ONE OF
    `s 173J(4)(a) a person attending a meeting`
    `s 173J(4)(b) a person present or personally present at a meeting`
    `s 173J(4)(c) a vote of a member at a meeting`
    `s 173J(4)(d) voting by a member at a meeting`
    `s 173J(4)(e) the entitlement or right of a person to vote at a meeting`
    `s 173J(4)(f) voting by a person on a show of hands`
    `s 173J(4)(g) the entitlement or right of a person to be heard at a meeting`
    `s 173J(4)(h) the right of a person to speak on a resolution before a meeting`
    `s 173J(4)(i) the right of a person to speak at a meeting`
    `s 173J(4)(j) members present at a meeting being at liberty to discuss any matter`
    `s 173J(4)(k) a representation being read out or a declaration being made at a meeting`
    `s 173J(4)(l) an auditor's report being read before the company in general meeting`
    `s 173J(4)(m) a document being available for inspection at a meeting`
    `s 173J(4)(n) the production of the company's register at the commencement of the annual general meeting and its keeping open and accessible`
    `s 173J(4)(o) the keeping of the list of members open and accessible during the meeting`
    `s 173J(4)(p) the laying of a statement or other document before a meeting`
    `s 173J(4)(q) a statement or other document being laid or caused to be laid before the company at a meeting`

-- src:15444 | (4) Unless excluded or modified under subsection (5) or excluded
-- src:15445 | under subsection (7), where a meeting to which this section applies is
-- src:15446 | held (whether wholly or partly) using virtual meeting technology —
-- src:15448 | (a) a reference in this Act to any person (including any
-- src:15449 | member of a company) attending a meeting includes a
-- src:15450 | person who is attending the meeting using virtual meeting
-- src:15451 | technology;
-- src:15453 | (b) a reference in this Act to any person (including any
-- src:15454 | member of a company) present or personally present at a
-- src:15455 | meeting includes a person who attends the meeting using
-- src:15456 | virtual meeting technology;
-- src:15458 | (c) subject to paragraph (f), a reference in this Act to a vote of a
-- src:15459 | member of a company at a meeting (including a vote for
-- src:15460 | the purposes of electing a chairperson of a meeting),
-- src:15461 | includes a vote by electronic means or any other means
-- src:15462 | permitted by the constitution of the company;
-- src:15464 | (d) subject to paragraph (f), a reference in this Act to voting by
-- src:15465 | a member of the company at a meeting (including voting
-- src:15466 | for the purposes of electing a chairperson of a meeting),
-- src:15467 | includes voting by electronic means or any other means
-- src:15468 | permitted by the constitution of the company;
-- src:15470 | (e) subject to paragraph (f), a reference in this Act to the
-- src:15471 | entitlement or right of a person to vote at a meeting
-- src:15472 | includes, where the person is present by virtual meeting
-- src:15473 | technology, the entitlement or right to vote by electronic
-- src:15474 | means or any other means permitted by the constitution of
-- src:15475 | the company;
-- src:15477 | (f) a reference in this Act to voting by a person on a show of
-- src:15478 | hands at a meeting includes, where the person is present by
-- src:15479 | virtual meeting technology, voting by the person by
-- src:15480 | electronic means or any other means permitted by the
-- src:15485 | constitution of the company but only if the person can be
-- src:15486 | identified —
-- src:15488 | (i) by any method that may be prescribed relating to the
-- src:15489 | verification or authentication of the identity of
-- src:15490 | persons attending the meeting; or
-- src:15492 | (ii) if no method is so prescribed, by any method that the
-- src:15493 | directors of the company may determine;
-- src:15495 | (g) a reference in this Act to the entitlement or right of a person
-- src:15496 | to be heard at a meeting includes, where the person is
-- src:15497 | present by virtual meeting technology, the entitlement or
-- src:15498 | right to be heard by any means of synchronous
-- src:15499 | communication that the directors of the company may
-- src:15500 | determine;
-- src:15502 | (h) a reference in this Act to the right of a person to speak on
-- src:15503 | any resolution before a meeting includes, where the person
-- src:15504 | is present by virtual meeting technology, the right to
-- src:15505 | communicate by any means of synchronous
-- src:15506 | communication that the directors of the company may
-- src:15507 | determine;
-- src:15509 | (i) a reference in this Act to the right of a person to speak at a
-- src:15510 | meeting includes, where the person is present by virtual
-- src:15511 | meeting technology, the right to communicate by any
-- src:15512 | means of synchronous communication that the directors of
-- src:15513 | the company may determine;
-- src:15515 | (j) a reference in this Act to members of a company present at
-- src:15516 | a meeting being at liberty to discuss any matter includes
-- src:15517 | the discussion by members present by virtual meeting
-- src:15518 | technology of the matter by any means of synchronous
-- src:15519 | communication that the directors of the company may
-- src:15520 | determine;
-- src:15522 | (k) a reference in this Act to any representation being read out
-- src:15523 | or declaration being made at a meeting includes the
-- src:15524 | communication of that representation or declaration at the
-- src:15525 | meeting by any means of synchronous communication that
-- src:15526 | the directors of the company may determine;
-- src:15531 | (l) a reference in this Act to an auditor’s report being read
-- src:15532 | before the company in general meeting includes the
-- src:15533 | communication of the contents of that auditor’s report at
-- src:15534 | the general meeting by any means of synchronous
-- src:15535 | communication that the directors of the company may
-- src:15536 | determine;
-- src:15538 | (m) a reference in this Act to a document being available for
-- src:15539 | inspection at a meeting includes making the document
-- src:15540 | available —
-- src:15542 | (i) on a website during the meeting; or
-- src:15544 | (ii) by any other means during the meeting that the
-- src:15545 | company may by ordinary resolution determine;
-- src:15547 | (n) a reference in this Act to the production of the company’s
-- src:15548 | register at the commencement of the annual general
-- src:15549 | meeting and to the keeping of the register open and
-- src:15550 | accessible during the meeting to all persons attending the
-- src:15551 | meeting includes making the register available —
-- src:15553 | (i) on a website during the meeting; or
-- src:15555 | (ii) by any other means during the meeting that the
-- src:15556 | company may by ordinary resolution determine;
-- src:15558 | (o) a reference in this Act to the keeping of the list showing the
-- src:15559 | names and addresses of the members of a company and the
-- src:15560 | number of shares held by them respectively open and
-- src:15561 | accessible to any member during the continuance of the
-- src:15562 | meeting includes making the list available —
-- src:15564 | (i) on a website during the meeting; or
-- src:15566 | (ii) by any other means during the meeting that the
-- src:15567 | company may by ordinary resolution determine;
-- src:15569 | (p) a reference in this Act to the laying of a statement, financial
-- src:15570 | statement, consolidated financial statement, balance sheet,
-- src:15571 | auditor’s report or other document before a meeting of the
-- src:15572 | company includes producing or making available the
-- src:15573 | relevant document —
-- src:15575 | (i) on a website; or
-- src:15580 | (ii) by any other means that the company may by
-- src:15581 | ordinary resolution determine; and
-- src:15583 | (q) a reference in this Act to any statement, financial
-- src:15584 | statement, consolidated financial statement, balance
-- src:15585 | sheet, auditor’s report or other document being laid or
-- src:15586 | caused to be laid before the company at a meeting includes
-- src:15587 | the relevant document being produced or made available or
-- src:15588 | caused to be produced or made available —
-- src:15590 | (i) on a website; or
-- src:15592 | (ii) by any other means that the company may by
-- src:15593 | ordinary resolution determine.
@ref s 173J(4) (src:15444-15593)
GIVEN paragraph IS A `s 173J(4) paragraph`
      `the meeting is held wholly or partly using virtual meeting technology` IS A BOOLEAN
      `subsection (5) excludes or modifies the paragraph, or subsection (7) excludes it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is present at the meeting using virtual meeting technology` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the means used is electronic means or any other means permitted by the constitution of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person can be identified by a method that is prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `no method is prescribed and the person can be identified by a method the directors of the company have determined` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the means used is a means of synchronous communication that the directors of the company have determined` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is made available during the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is made available on a website` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is made available by other means that the company has determined by ordinary resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 173J(4) the reference includes the virtual form of what it names` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the meeting is held wholly or partly using virtual meeting technology`) OR `subsection (5) excludes or modifies the paragraph, or subsection (7) excludes it`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Unless excluded or modified under subsection (5) or excluded under subsection (7), where a meeting to which this section applies is held (whether wholly or partly) using virtual meeting technology" (the gate fails; the interpretive provision's own question)
    ELSE CONSIDER paragraph
         WHEN `s 173J(4)(a) a person attending a meeting` THEN
              IF `the person is present at the meeting using virtual meeting technology` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "includes a person who is attending the meeting using virtual meeting technology"
         WHEN `s 173J(4)(b) a person present or personally present at a meeting` THEN
              IF `the person is present at the meeting using virtual meeting technology` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "includes a person who attends the meeting using virtual meeting technology"
         WHEN `s 173J(4)(c) a vote of a member at a meeting` THEN
              IF `the means used is electronic means or any other means permitted by the constitution of the company` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "includes a vote by electronic means or any other means permitted by the constitution"
         WHEN `s 173J(4)(d) voting by a member at a meeting` THEN
              IF `the means used is electronic means or any other means permitted by the constitution of the company` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "includes voting by electronic means or any other means permitted by the constitution"
         WHEN `s 173J(4)(e) the entitlement or right of a person to vote at a meeting` THEN
              IF `the person is present at the meeting using virtual meeting technology` AND `the means used is electronic means or any other means permitted by the constitution of the company`
              THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "includes, where the person is present by virtual meeting technology, the entitlement or right to vote by electronic means or any other means permitted by the constitution"
         WHEN `s 173J(4)(f) voting by a person on a show of hands` THEN
              IF NOT (`the person is present at the meeting using virtual meeting technology` AND `the means used is electronic means or any other means permitted by the constitution of the company`)
              THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "includes, where the person is present by virtual meeting technology, voting by the person by electronic means or any other means permitted by the constitution"
              ELSE (IF `the person can be identified by a method that is prescribed` OR `no method is prescribed and the person can be identified by a method the directors of the company have determined`
                    THEN JUST TRUE
                    ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but only if the person can be identified (i) by any method that may be prescribed ...; or (ii) if no method is so prescribed, by any method that the directors of the company may determine"
         WHEN `s 173J(4)(g) the entitlement or right of a person to be heard at a meeting` THEN
              IF `the person is present at the meeting using virtual meeting technology` AND `the means used is a means of synchronous communication that the directors of the company have determined`
              THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "includes, where the person is present by virtual meeting technology, the entitlement or right to be heard by any means of synchronous communication that the directors of the company may determine"
         WHEN `s 173J(4)(h) the right of a person to speak on a resolution before a meeting` THEN
              IF `the person is present at the meeting using virtual meeting technology` AND `the means used is a means of synchronous communication that the directors of the company have determined`
              THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "includes, where the person is present by virtual meeting technology, the right to communicate by any means of synchronous communication that the directors of the company may determine"
         WHEN `s 173J(4)(i) the right of a person to speak at a meeting` THEN
              IF `the person is present at the meeting using virtual meeting technology` AND `the means used is a means of synchronous communication that the directors of the company have determined`
              THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "includes, where the person is present by virtual meeting technology, the right to communicate by any means of synchronous communication that the directors of the company may determine"
         WHEN `s 173J(4)(j) members present at a meeting being at liberty to discuss any matter` THEN
              IF `the person is present at the meeting using virtual meeting technology` AND `the means used is a means of synchronous communication that the directors of the company have determined`
              THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "includes the discussion by members present by virtual meeting technology of the matter by any means of synchronous communication that the directors of the company may determine"
         WHEN `s 173J(4)(k) a representation being read out or a declaration being made at a meeting` THEN
              IF `the means used is a means of synchronous communication that the directors of the company have determined` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "includes the communication of that representation or declaration at the meeting by any means of synchronous communication that the directors of the company may determine"
         WHEN `s 173J(4)(l) an auditor's report being read before the company in general meeting` THEN
              IF `the means used is a means of synchronous communication that the directors of the company have determined` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "includes the communication of the contents of that auditor's report at the general meeting by any means of synchronous communication that the directors of the company may determine"
         WHEN `s 173J(4)(m) a document being available for inspection at a meeting` THEN
              IF `the document is made available during the meeting` AND (`the document is made available on a website` OR `the document is made available by other means that the company has determined by ordinary resolution`)
              THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "includes making the document available (i) on a website during the meeting; or (ii) by any other means during the meeting that the company may by ordinary resolution determine"
         WHEN `s 173J(4)(n) the production of the company's register at the commencement of the annual general meeting and its keeping open and accessible` THEN
              IF `the document is made available during the meeting` AND (`the document is made available on a website` OR `the document is made available by other means that the company has determined by ordinary resolution`)
              THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "includes making the register available (i) on a website during the meeting; or (ii) by any other means during the meeting that the company may by ordinary resolution determine"
         WHEN `s 173J(4)(o) the keeping of the list of members open and accessible during the meeting` THEN
              IF `the document is made available during the meeting` AND (`the document is made available on a website` OR `the document is made available by other means that the company has determined by ordinary resolution`)
              THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "includes making the list available (i) on a website during the meeting; or (ii) by any other means during the meeting that the company may by ordinary resolution determine"
         WHEN `s 173J(4)(p) the laying of a statement or other document before a meeting` THEN
              IF `the document is made available on a website` OR `the document is made available by other means that the company has determined by ordinary resolution`
              THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "includes producing or making available the relevant document (i) on a website; or (ii) by any other means that the company may by ordinary resolution determine"
         WHEN `s 173J(4)(q) a statement or other document being laid or caused to be laid before the company at a meeting` THEN
              IF `the document is made available on a website` OR `the document is made available by other means that the company has determined by ordinary resolution`
              THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "includes the relevant document being produced or made available ... (i) on a website; or (ii) by any other means that the company may by ordinary resolution determine"

§ `Section 173J(5): when the section yields to the constitution`

`s 173J(5) the day 1 July 2023` MEANS Date 1 7 2023

-- (5): the section "applies despite the provisions contained in a company's constitution, except where" the constitution excludes (2)(b) or (c) or excludes
-- or modifies (4). For a company incorporated before 1 July 2023 only an amendment made on or after that date counts ((a)); for one incorporated on or
-- after it the constitution as first registered counts as well as any later amendment ((b)(i) and (ii)). The input `the date the exclusion or modification
-- took effect in the constitution` is, for a term of the constitution as first registered, the date of incorporation.
-- src:15595 | (5) This section applies despite the provisions contained in a
-- src:15596 | company’s constitution, except where —
-- src:15598 | (a) in the case of a company incorporated before 1 July 2023,
-- src:15599 | the company on or after that date amends, alters or adds to
-- src:15600 | its constitution —
-- src:15602 | (i) to exclude the application of paragraph (b) or (c) of
-- src:15603 | subsection (2) (or both) in respect of all or any
-- src:15604 | meetings to which this section applies; or
-- src:15606 | (ii) to exclude or modify the application of paragraphs
-- src:15607 | (a) to (q) of subsection (4) (or any of those
-- src:15608 | paragraphs) in respect of all or any meetings to
-- src:15609 | which this section applies; or
-- src:15611 | (b) in the case of a company incorporated on or after 1 July
-- src:15612 | 2023 —
-- src:15614 | (i) the constitution of the company —
-- src:15616 | (A) excludes the application of paragraph (b) or (c)
-- src:15617 | of subsection (2) (or both) in respect of all or
-- src:15618 | any meetings to which this section applies; or
-- src:15620 | (B) excludes or modifies the application of
-- src:15621 | paragraphs (a) to (q) of subsection (4) (or
-- src:15622 | any of those paragraphs) in respect of all or any
-- src:15623 | meetings to which this section applies; or
-- src:15628 | (ii) the company at any time after its incorporation
-- src:15629 | amends, alters or adds to its constitution —
-- src:15631 | (A) to exclude the application of paragraph (b) or
-- src:15632 | (c) of subsection (2) (or both) in respect of all
-- src:15633 | or any meetings to which this section applies;
-- src:15634 | or
-- src:15636 | (B) to exclude or modify the application of
-- src:15637 | paragraphs (a) to (q) of subsection (4) (or
-- src:15638 | any of those paragraphs) in respect of all or any
-- src:15639 | meetings to which this section applies.
@ref s 173J(5) (src:15595-15639)
GIVEN `the date the company was incorporated` IS A DATE
      `the date the exclusion or modification took effect in the constitution` IS A DATE
      `the constitution excludes the application of paragraph (b) or (c) of subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the constitution excludes or modifies the application of paragraphs (a) to (q) of subsection (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 173J(5) the constitution excludes or modifies the section` MEANS
    IF    (`the constitution excludes the application of paragraph (b) or (c) of subsection (2)` OR `the constitution excludes or modifies the application of paragraphs (a) to (q) of subsection (4)`)
      AND (    `the date the company was incorporated` AT LEAST `s 173J(5) the day 1 July 2023`
            OR `the date the exclusion or modification took effect in the constitution` AT LEAST `s 173J(5) the day 1 July 2023`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies despite the provisions contained in a company's constitution, except where" -- no listed exception holds, so the section is not excluded

§ `Section 173J(6) to (8)`

-- src:15641 | (6) In subsection (4), a reference to a member of a company
-- src:15642 | includes, where appropriate, the member’s proxy or the member’s
-- src:15643 | representative.
@ref s 173J(6) (src:15641-15643)
GIVEN `the person is the member's proxy or the member's representative` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is appropriate to read the reference to a member as including the proxy or the representative` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 173J(6) the reference to a member in subsection (4) includes the person` MEANS
    IF `the person is the member's proxy or the member's representative` AND `it is appropriate to read the reference to a member as including the proxy or the representative`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "a reference to a member of a company includes, where appropriate, the member's proxy or the member's representative"

-- (8): "To avoid doubt and subject to the constitution of the company, nothing in this Act prohibits a meeting of the board of directors of a company, or a committee
-- consisting of one or more directors of a company, from being held (a) at a physical place and using virtual meeting technology; or (b) using virtual meeting technology only."
-- The function answers for this Act only; whether the constitution prohibits it is a separate question the text leaves to the constitution.
-- src:15649 | (8) To avoid doubt and subject to the constitution of the company,
-- src:15650 | nothing in this Act prohibits a meeting of the board of directors of a
-- src:15651 | company, or a committee consisting of one or more directors of a
-- src:15652 | company, from being held —
-- src:15654 | (a) at a physical place and using virtual meeting technology; or
-- src:15656 | (b) using virtual meeting technology only.
@ref s 173J(8) (src:15649-15656)
GIVEN `the meeting is a meeting of the board of directors of the company, or of a committee consisting of one or more directors of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the meeting is held at a physical place and using virtual meeting technology, or using virtual meeting technology only` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 173J(8) this Act prohibits the board or committee meeting from being held in the way` MEANS
    IF `the meeting is a meeting of the board of directors of the company, or of a committee consisting of one or more directors of the company` AND `the meeting is held at a physical place and using virtual meeting technology, or using virtual meeting technology only`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "nothing in this Act prohibits a meeting of the board of directors of a company, or a committee consisting of one or more directors of a company, from being held (a) ...; or (b) ..." (a flat negative)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection speaks of board and committee meetings held in those two ways and says nothing of other meetings or ways
